r a vowel use 를, after a consonant use 을."}, {"id": "e3", "isTarget": true, "correct_rabbit": ["마셔요"], "correct_turtle": ["마셔요"], "turtle_explanation": "Keep '마셔요' as one block — it is not this lesson's focus."}], "options": [{"id": "o1", "text": "을", "mode": "turtle"}, {"id": "o2", "text": "저는", "mode": "rabbit"}, {"id": "o3", "text": "저는", "mode": "turtle"}, {"id": "o4", "text": "물을", "mode": "rabbit"}, {"id": "o5", "text": "마셔요", "mode": "rabbit"}, {"id": "o6", "text": "물", "mode": "turtle"}, {"id": "o7", "text": "마셔요", "mode": "turtle"}, {"id": "o8", "text": "를", "mode": "turtle"}, {"id": "o9", "text": "물를", "mode": "rabbit"}]}}, {"step_type": "completion", "title": "Lesson 3 Mastered!", "instruction": "Great! You can now say what you like in Korean.", "content": {"text": "You've learned '저는 [thing]을/를 좋아해요.'\nConsonant ending → 을 (빵을), vowel ending → 를 (커피를).", "highlights": ["을", "를"]}}]}$lsn$::jsonb
